#!/bin/bash
# Feature-independence loop — self-paced; new session: /loop $(tail -1 FEATURE_INDEP_LOOP.sh)
# Roadmap: docs/FEATURE_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP.md (pattern §0, anchors §1, constraints §2, measured state §3, ledger §4)
# Harness: cd apps/market-ui && npx playwright test featureContinuity --config=playwright.config.ts

Read docs/FEATURE_INDEPENDENCE_ROADMAP.md and follow its pattern and hard constraints exactly. Do only the first unchecked [ ] task in Section 4; that task's Accept line is the acceptance test. GOAL: the feature keeps running when the user switches views and, on return, resumes the SAME in-flight session with live progress — never restarts it, never shows nothing, never duplicates it. Do NOT invent a new mechanism: two features already do this correctly and are the template — read stores/researchStore.ts + SearchPage research mode, and stores/gridRunStore.ts + GridView, and copy that exact shape (module-level Zustand store keyed by session id; the async loop writes to the store; the run is aborted ONLY by explicit user action, never by a useEffect cleanup; the component is a pure view that re-attaches on remount). The just-completed FI-1 (stores/companyBriefStore.ts + CompanyBrief.tsx) is a worked example keyed by ticker — mirror it. Before writing code, re-measure the target feature against the current code and against prod rather than trusting Section 3, which is a dated snapshot; if a measurement disagrees, the fresh measurement wins and you correct Section 3 in the same commit. Every lifted run must register a job in backgroundStore (start on run, end in finally) so the global BackgroundActivity indicator shows it, and clicking the job returns to the feature's view. Respect that navigation must be CLIENT-SIDE to preserve the in-memory store — the continuity spec proves this by clicking a nav Link or the indicator job, never page.goto (a full reload wipes the store, which is expected and not a bug). No new npm deps (Zustand is already present; check package.json). A task is done only when: its Accept line is demonstrably satisfied by a real run, npx tsc -b is clean from apps/market-ui, its new continuity spec plus e2e/featureContinuity.spec.ts pass via npx playwright test, and the existing guards e2e/tnNullFeed.spec.ts + e2e/hubAssetMarket.spec.ts + e2e/backgroundActivity.spec.ts stayed green, and vercel --prod from repo root ran (these are UI changes). Then flip the ledger line to [x], append ONE Section 5 progress-log row with REAL numbers from that run (which specs passed, tsc error count — no adjectives), and commit on roadmap/world-class with message "feat(feature-indep): FI-n <what> - <verify>" (use git commit -F file; apostrophes in a -m string break the shell). Never git push unless asked. PERSISTENCE: never end the loop on a usage or rate limit or 429 or overload - stop consuming tokens immediately, ScheduleWakeup 3600s with this exact /loop prompt, and on wake re-read the ledger plus progress log and resume the same task from its last verified step; log partial progress BEFORE long or risky operations. Only stop for: no [ ] remaining in Section 4, or a task blocked on user-only input such as credentials or a dead upstream feed - then say exactly what is needed, note it in the ledger, skip to the next unblocked [ ] task if one exists, and only if ALL remaining tasks are blocked ScheduleWakeup 3600s so the loop resumes when unblocked.
